1007
00:34:09,304 --> 00:34:11,499
- It now comes to light that both of you,

1008
00:34:11,499 --> 00:34:15,018
over the past 18 years,
have proven yourselves

1009
00:34:15,018 --> 00:34:16,421
utterly incompetent.

1010
00:34:16,421 --> 00:34:18,422
- [Crow] Thank you.

1011
00:34:18,422 --> 00:34:19,691
- With the most important responsibility

1012
00:34:19,691 --> 00:34:20,965
given to a man and his wife.

1013
00:34:20,965 --> 00:34:22,342
- [Crow] Sir, it's one parking ticket.

1014
00:34:22,342 --> 00:34:26,377
- I refer to the bringing up
of children in your own home.

1015
00:34:26,377 --> 00:34:28,627
- [Tom] Honey, don't laugh.

1016
00:34:29,544 --> 00:34:30,879
- In all fairness

1017
00:34:30,879 --> 00:34:32,155
(crew loud snoring noises)

1018
00:34:32,155 --> 00:34:34,712
to the society which
you so miserably failed,

1019
00:34:34,712 --> 00:34:36,137
an injustice to this child.

1020
00:34:36,137 --> 00:34:38,030
(crew loud snoring)

1021
00:34:38,030 --> 00:34:40,021
I must deny your request.

1022
00:34:40,021 --> 00:34:42,586
- [Tom] By the way, you're
ugly and stupid, too.

1023
00:34:42,586 --> 00:34:44,542
- [Woman in Hat] How am I to blame?

1024
00:34:44,542 --> 00:34:46,641
Where could I have failed?

1025
00:34:46,641 --> 00:34:48,996
I remember I gave her
everything she ever wanted.

1026
00:34:48,996 --> 00:34:51,363
- [Crow] Her neck is having a flashback.

1027
00:34:51,363 --> 00:34:52,901
- [Voiceover] Everything.

1028
00:34:52,901 --> 00:34:55,347
- [Tom] Ladies and gentlemen,
your screenwriter, Ed Wood.

1029
00:34:55,347 --> 00:34:56,694
- Hi, Mom.

1030
00:34:56,694 --> 00:34:58,344
- [Tom] Can I have more of everything?

1031
00:34:58,344 --> 00:35:00,695
- Got time to talk a minute,
it's rather important.

1032
00:35:00,695 --> 00:35:03,437
- Good gracious, no, I'm
an hour late already.

1033
00:35:03,437 --> 00:35:04,471
- [Crow] I'm two weeks late.

1034
00:35:04,471 --> 00:35:07,653
- I've gotta be first and all
that sort of thing, you know.

1035
00:35:07,653 --> 00:35:10,039
Besides, what can be so important

1036
00:35:10,039 --> 00:35:11,507
in your young life as to

1037
00:35:11,507 --> 00:35:13,277
warrant my attention so drastically?

1038
00:35:13,277 --> 00:35:14,110
- [Mike] Wow.

1039
00:35:14,110 --> 00:35:14,943
- Well, it's been a long time

1040
00:35:14,943 --> 00:35:16,210
since we had a heart to heart talk.

1041
00:35:16,210 --> 00:35:17,636
- There, there, it can wait.

1042
00:35:17,636 --> 00:35:18,730
- [Crow] Go away.

1043
00:35:18,730 --> 00:35:22,350
- Besides, what can be more
important than our charities?

1044
00:35:22,350 --> 00:35:24,481
So many children and needy families.

1045
00:35:24,481 --> 00:35:25,513
- [Crow] Really bugs me.

1046
00:35:25,513 --> 00:35:27,578
- We're so busy this time of year.

1047
00:35:27,578 --> 00:35:29,928
And it's very, very important.

1048
00:35:29,928 --> 00:35:31,648
- I guess you're right, Mother.

1049
00:35:31,648 --> 00:35:32,481
- Of course I am.

1050
00:35:32,481 --> 00:35:33,997
- [Crow] Now, go do some crimes.

1051
00:35:33,997 --> 00:35:35,625
- Thank you, darling.

1052
00:35:35,625 --> 00:35:36,807
Tell you a secret.

1053
00:35:36,807 --> 00:35:37,710
- [Mike] I hate you.

1054
00:35:37,710 --> 00:35:39,271
- I think I like it down
at the club so much,

1055
00:35:39,271 --> 00:35:41,880
because I keep getting such nice flattery.

1056
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:42,993
The girls are always saying,

1057
00:35:42,993 --> 00:35:46,062
my, my, how young and pretty you look.

1058
00:35:46,062 --> 00:35:47,191
- [Tom] For an old hag.

1059
00:35:47,191 --> 00:35:48,979
- With you an 18-year-old daughter.

1060
00:35:48,979 --> 00:35:50,423
- But, you are pretty, mother.

1061
00:35:50,423 --> 00:35:51,938
- Oh, go along with you.

1062
00:35:51,938 --> 00:35:54,025
But, it does sound good.

1063
00:35:54,025 --> 00:35:55,698
Got a date tonight?

1064
00:35:55,698 --> 00:35:57,763
- Well, sort of.

1065
00:35:57,763 --> 00:36:00,149
- Oh, you pretty one, of course you do.

1066
00:36:00,149 --> 00:36:02,061
But, what night lately haven't you?

1067
00:36:02,061 --> 00:36:02,894
- [Mike] Watch 227.

1068
00:36:02,894 --> 00:36:04,679
- You come in as late as you have been,

1069
00:36:04,679 --> 00:36:06,734
do be careful and not make any noise.

1070
00:36:06,734 --> 00:36:07,567
- Dad?

1071
00:36:07,567 --> 00:36:09,086
- Oh, don't get me wrong,

1072
00:36:09,086 --> 00:36:10,710
he hasn't complained, or said anything.

1073
00:36:10,710 --> 00:36:11,903
- [Tom] In fact, he
hasn't moved in a week.

1074
00:36:11,903 --> 00:36:14,212
- The poor man works so hard.

1075
00:36:14,212 --> 00:36:16,472
That newspaper will be the death of him.

1076
00:36:16,472 --> 00:36:17,968
- [Crow] His route is killing him.

1077
00:36:17,968 --> 00:36:19,951
- Do be a dear and take
care when you come in?

1078
00:36:19,951 --> 00:36:21,890
He needs what little rest he can get.

1079
00:36:21,890 --> 00:36:23,000
- [Tom] It got rough last night.

1080
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,266
- Thank goodness you aren't one of those

1081
00:36:24,266 --> 00:36:26,065
character types that your father's paper

1082
00:36:26,065 --> 00:36:28,148
is always printing about.

1083
00:36:29,035 --> 00:36:31,222
- Need some mad money?

1084
00:36:31,222 --> 00:36:32,688
Or is he a gentleman?

1085
00:36:32,688 --> 00:36:33,775
- I have enough, Mother.

1086
00:36:33,775 --> 00:36:35,339
- Don't be silly.

1087
00:36:35,339 --> 00:36:36,394
There's never enough.

1088
00:36:36,394 --> 00:36:38,297
- [Tom] Please, no more,
not again, my life is hell.

1089
00:36:38,297 --> 00:36:40,728
Enough, no more money.

1090
00:36:40,728 --> 00:36:42,173
- You left the amount blank again.

1091
00:36:42,173 --> 00:36:45,912
I could be mean and fill
it in for a fortune.

1092
00:36:45,912 --> 00:36:47,547
- You could, but you won't.

1093
00:36:47,547 --> 00:36:48,865
Let me know how much you make it out for,

1094
00:36:48,865 --> 00:36:50,593
so that I can keep my
bank balance straight.

1095
00:36:50,593 --> 00:36:51,442
- All right, Mother.

1096
00:36:51,442 --> 00:36:53,072
Will you be using my car again, tonight?

1097
00:36:53,072 --> 00:36:54,797
- If you don't mind, dear.

1098
00:36:54,797 --> 00:36:56,825
You can use mine.

1099
00:36:56,825 --> 00:36:58,019
- Now I'll tell you a secret.

1100
00:36:58,019 --> 00:36:58,852
- [Tom] This doesn't make sense.

1101
00:36:58,852 --> 00:37:00,241
- There are times I like yours better.

1102
00:37:00,241 --> 00:37:02,063
Tonight is one of those times.

1103
00:37:02,063 --> 00:37:04,624
- [Crow] Keep your life
to yourself, honey.

1104
00:37:04,624 --> 00:37:07,041
One googolplex, and 79 cents.

1105
00:37:12,848 --> 00:37:14,434
- [Crow] Oh, my life is hell.

1106
00:37:14,434 --> 00:37:16,359
How much more of this can I take?

1107
00:37:16,359 --> 00:37:19,776
I'm going to report her child protection.

1108
00:37:21,130 --> 00:37:22,028
- [Tom] Hello.

1109
00:37:22,028 --> 00:37:23,768
- Phil, this is Paul.

1110
00:37:23,768 --> 00:37:24,601
- [Tom] Paul?

1111
00:37:24,601 --> 00:37:25,434
- Is everything ready?

1112
00:37:25,434 --> 00:37:26,267
- [Tom] Who is this?

1113
00:37:26,267 --> 00:37:28,848
- Good, George and Gerry show yet?

1114
00:37:28,848 --> 00:37:29,681
- [Tom] Paul?

1115
00:37:29,681 --> 00:37:31,047
- Stop worrying, they'll get to you.

1116
00:37:31,047 --> 00:37:31,937
- [Tom] But, I don't know any Paul.

1117
00:37:31,937 --> 00:37:33,390
- I'll be along as soon as I get dressed.

1118
00:37:33,390 --> 00:37:34,774
- Mother just this minute left.

1119
00:37:34,774 --> 00:37:38,269
- [Tom] But, who's Paul, I don't know any.

1120
00:37:38,269 --> 00:37:42,430
Think I'll throw pig's blood on the wall.

1121
00:37:42,430 --> 00:37:43,840
- [Crow] Think of the hellish life.

1122
00:37:43,840 --> 00:37:45,451
Your mother writing you blank checks.

1123
00:37:45,451 --> 00:37:48,936
But does that justify going
out and making right turns?

1124
00:37:48,936 --> 00:37:49,873
No, I say to you.

1125
00:37:49,873 --> 00:37:53,040
- [Tom] Society owes me a Kit Kat bar.

1126
00:37:54,834 --> 00:37:56,339
- [Crow] Rosewood Super Service.

1127
00:37:56,339 --> 00:38:00,027
Soon to be, Rosewood's Lickity Lube.

1128
00:38:00,027 --> 00:38:02,680
- [Tom] Every minute away
from my porno mags is hell.

1129
00:38:02,680 --> 00:38:07,219
Good evening, it's my
pleasure to serve you, hey.

1130
00:38:07,219 --> 00:38:08,693
- [Crow] Huh, Benazir
Bhutto is holding him up.

1131
00:38:08,693 --> 00:38:12,276
(dramatic orchestra music)

1132
00:38:13,223 --> 00:38:16,310
(Tom hums dramatic music)

1133
00:38:16,310 --> 00:38:20,477
- [Tom] There's a free oil
filter with every fill up.

1134
00:38:22,567 --> 00:38:26,687
Hey, do we want the Ridged Tool calender?

1135
00:38:26,687 --> 00:38:28,687
- [Mike] Ooh, left turn.

1136
00:38:31,881 --> 00:38:35,342
- [Tom] You can trust our octanes.

1137
00:38:35,342 --> 00:38:36,759
Check your hoses?

1138
00:38:41,312 --> 00:38:43,979
Need an area map, we got plenty.

1139
00:38:45,091 --> 00:38:48,711
Hello girls, good luck with the hold up.

1140
00:38:48,711 --> 00:38:52,084
Saw your mom in here the other day.

1141
00:38:52,084 --> 00:38:55,904
(dramatic orchestra music)

1142
00:38:55,904 --> 00:38:59,692
- [Mike] Let's go, we've got
all the barrel of fun snacks.

1143
00:38:59,692 --> 00:39:03,363
- [Tom] Please, take an air freshener.

1144
00:39:03,363 --> 00:39:04,196
(Thud)

1145
00:39:04,196 --> 00:39:06,566
I'll just go ahead and fall, then.

1146
00:39:06,566 --> 00:39:09,066
(Mike laughs)

1147
00:39:10,034 --> 00:39:12,017
- [Tom] Hey, your rear
tire is a little low.

1148
00:39:12,017 --> 00:39:13,294
- [Crow] Ding ding.

1149
00:39:13,294 --> 00:39:14,393
Ding ding.

1150
00:39:14,393 --> 00:39:16,310
Was the restroom clean?

1151
00:39:18,893 --> 00:39:22,393
(upbeat electronic music)

1152
00:39:26,935 --> 00:39:27,930
- [Tom] Well, I did a c-section,

1153
00:39:27,930 --> 00:39:29,918
but I was unable to find anything.

1154
00:39:29,918 --> 00:39:31,576
- [Man Black Suit] Will
he pull through, doc?

1155
00:39:31,576 --> 00:39:33,144
- He hasn't regained consciousness,

1156
00:39:33,144 --> 00:39:34,955
and it's top heavy odds he ever will.

1157
00:39:34,955 --> 00:39:35,944
- [Man Black Suit] Pretty bad, huh?

1158
00:39:35,944 --> 00:39:36,906
- Pretty bad.

1159
00:39:36,906 --> 00:39:39,000
- These fool kids, when will they learn.

1160
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:40,202
- These aren't kids.

1161
00:39:40,202 --> 00:39:41,939
These are morons.

1162
00:39:41,939 --> 00:39:44,689
- [Crow] Will he ever pump again?

1163
00:39:45,897 --> 00:39:47,108
- [Man Dark Suit] Hi, Barney

1164
00:39:47,108 --> 00:39:48,636
- Lieutenant, Tom, doctor.

1165
00:39:48,636 --> 00:39:49,469
- [Mike] Honey.

1166
00:39:49,469 --> 00:39:50,302
- [Crow] Peep Peep.

1167
00:39:50,302 --> 00:39:51,135
- [Tom] Cookie.

1168
00:39:51,135 --> 00:39:51,983
- Pretty bad one this time.

1169
00:39:51,983 --> 00:39:53,103
How about it, doc.

1170
00:39:53,103 --> 00:39:54,181
- Pretty bad.

1171
00:39:54,181 --> 00:39:56,236
I'll get back to you later
if there's any change.

1172
00:39:56,236 --> 00:39:58,669
- [Mike] Aw, he said he'd give
me a deal on wiper blades.

1173
00:39:58,669 --> 00:39:59,915
- [Man In Hat] Anything I can print?

1174
00:39:59,915 --> 00:40:02,403
- You heard the doctor, nothing.

1175
00:40:02,403 --> 00:40:03,864
- Suppose it's the same gang?

1176
00:40:03,864 --> 00:40:05,378
- Chances are.

1177
00:40:05,378 --> 00:40:07,059
If only he comes to, then we'll be--

1178
00:40:07,059 --> 00:40:08,081
- Well if it is the same gang,

1179
00:40:08,081 --> 00:40:09,952
that brings their record to 17.

1180
00:40:09,952 --> 00:40:12,143
- And the last 7 of them
have been gas stations.

1181
00:40:12,143 --> 00:40:12,976
- [Mike] Any pattern?

1182
00:40:12,976 --> 00:40:14,448
- Looks like they'll make
a specialty of gas stations

1183
00:40:14,448 --> 00:40:15,577
for a while now.

1184
00:40:15,577 --> 00:40:17,202
- If they do, we may be ready for them.

1185
00:40:17,202 --> 00:40:18,119
- How do you mean?

1186
00:40:18,119 --> 00:40:19,043
- [Crow] Well, we'll prepare ourselves.

1187
00:40:19,043 --> 00:40:20,508
- All gas stations open after 10 pm

1188
00:40:20,508 --> 00:40:24,304
will be warned to have two
men on duty at all times.

1189
00:40:24,304 --> 00:40:27,838
One of those men could be a policeman.

1190
00:40:27,838 --> 00:40:29,181
- [Tom] Well, I tried to jump start him.

1191
00:40:29,181 --> 00:40:30,598
That didn't work.

1192
00:40:32,321 --> 00:40:35,612
- Lieutenant, I left Dr. Ryan in charge.

1193
00:40:35,612 --> 00:40:38,810
The man was lucky, he'll pull through.

1194
00:40:38,810 --> 00:40:41,542
- [Crow] Well, let's just
let the scene peter out.

1195
00:40:41,542 --> 00:40:43,625
(laughs)

1196
00:40:45,410 --> 00:40:46,725
- [Tom] All but the Teutonic races

1197
00:40:46,725 --> 00:40:48,453
will never be capable of leadership,

1198
00:40:48,453 --> 00:40:49,952
and yet they breed rapidly like

1199
00:40:49,952 --> 00:40:54,440
the mongrels that they, oh
(clears throat) more later.

1200
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:55,673
- Hi Chief.

1201
00:40:55,673 --> 00:40:56,852
- Oh, hello, Barney.

1202
00:40:56,852 --> 00:40:58,029
- [Mike] Where's your big purple suit?

1203
00:40:58,029 --> 00:40:59,263
- What's the matter?

1204
00:40:59,263 --> 00:41:01,033
- Oh, I'm tired, but no more than you.

1205
00:41:01,033 --> 00:41:02,028
- Yeah.

1206
00:41:02,028 --> 00:41:03,755
- [Crow] I mean you look really bad.

1207
00:41:03,755 --> 00:41:06,519
- Too much to newspapers these days.

1208
00:41:06,519 --> 00:41:07,842
- I haven't seen my
daughter, Paula, in a week.

1209
00:41:07,842 --> 00:41:10,420
I ran into her up at
school earlier this week.

1210
00:41:10,420 --> 00:41:11,253
- [Tom] Well, stalked her.

1211
00:41:11,253 --> 00:41:13,217
- She gets more beautiful every day.

1212
00:41:13,217 --> 00:41:15,285
- Like I said, I wouldn't know.

1213
00:41:15,285 --> 00:41:18,329
- One of these days, I'm
gonna take a day off.

1214
00:41:18,329 --> 00:41:21,134
- Maybe get to know her again.

1215
00:41:21,134 --> 00:41:22,214
- [Crow] Nah, who am I kidding.

1216
00:41:22,214 --> 00:41:23,649
- What happened down at the hospital?

1217
00:41:23,649 --> 00:41:26,138
- Well, the gas station
attendant pulled through.

1218
00:41:26,138 --> 00:41:27,281
- [Crow] Good, I need gas.

1219
00:41:27,281 --> 00:41:28,395
- He'll spend a couple
weeks in the hospital,

1220
00:41:28,395 --> 00:41:29,228
but he'll live.

1221
00:41:29,228 --> 00:41:30,893
- How much could he tell?

1222
00:41:30,893 --> 00:41:31,981
- It was the same gang.

1223
00:41:31,981 --> 00:41:32,814
- [Tom] Whoa.

1224
00:41:32,814 --> 00:41:35,835
- Wore masks, Levi's, leather jackets.

1225
00:41:35,835 --> 00:41:36,862
- [Mike] Looked like your daughter.

1226
00:41:36,862 --> 00:41:38,826
- Gloves, with a handful of guns.

1227
00:41:38,826 --> 00:41:41,702
- [Chief] Same bunch,
probably the same clues.

1228
00:41:41,702 --> 00:41:43,407
- [Mike] Who's that on the wall, Chopin?

1229
00:41:43,407 --> 00:41:45,705
- Well, no fingerprints, '55 sedan,

1230
00:41:45,705 --> 00:41:46,910
- [Mike] Schubert?

1231
00:41:46,910 --> 00:41:49,960
- Licence unknown, masks,
caps covering their hair,

1232
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:51,494
same old routine.

1233
00:41:51,494 --> 00:41:54,411
- Well, our little gang has
one thing in their favor.

1234
00:41:54,411 --> 00:41:55,646
- [Barney] Yeah, what's that?

1235
00:41:55,646 --> 00:41:56,847
- They haven't killed anyone.

1236
00:41:56,847 --> 00:41:57,878
(crew laughs)

1237
00:41:57,878 --> 00:41:59,087
- Yet.

1238
00:41:59,087 --> 00:42:00,843
- That's not their fault,
they've tried hard enough.

1239
00:42:00,843 --> 00:42:01,959
- [Crow] Maybe it's Sting?

1240
00:42:01,959 --> 00:42:02,792
- [Mike] Sting, yeah.

1241
00:42:02,792 --> 00:42:04,547
- [Chief] Too bad we
can't do anything about

1242
00:42:04,547 --> 00:42:07,186
giving them a little more time.

1243
00:42:07,186 --> 00:42:09,282
However, they happen to be news.

1244
00:42:09,282 --> 00:42:10,115
- [Mike] Thank you, Ben Bradley.

1245
00:42:10,115 --> 00:42:11,598
- You stick with the police department.

1246
00:42:11,598 --> 00:42:12,794
See this this thing through.

1247
00:42:12,794 --> 00:42:14,388
- [Mike] I'm going back to sleep.

1248
00:42:14,388 --> 00:42:15,672
- You're the boss, chief.

1249
00:42:15,672 --> 00:42:16,901
- [Crow] We gotta get this story out,

1250
00:42:16,901 --> 00:42:19,643
by, oh, next week is fine.

1251
00:42:19,643 --> 00:42:23,810
- [Tom] Rosicrucian are
growing nearer, I smelled.

1252
00:42:25,318 --> 00:42:30,238
- [Crow] Hey, that's the
same right turn as before.

1253
00:42:30,238 --> 00:42:32,811
Tom McKay Hill says, the big 55 Caddie

1254
00:42:32,811 --> 00:42:33,894
rides smooth.

1255
00:42:38,167 --> 00:42:41,584
Oh the passion, I find you so acceptable.

1256
00:42:42,887 --> 00:42:45,720
